.................
.................
STEP 0 of creating a new ADK/<new_dir> set of files -- Creating directory & copying some files.
.................
.................
A. cp -r 4.<current_number>  4.<next_number>
   For the rest of the instructions below, these are called 4.<old_number> and 4.<new_number> respectively.

B. Change techlib_adk.tnt/current to point to 4.<new_number> but do NOT tci until regressions clean and updated:
   ln -sfn 4.<new_number>  current

.................
.................
STEP 1 of creating a new ADK set of files
.................
.................

Edit 4.<new_number>/verilog/adk.v
to create any new modules.

Editing the Liberty is explained in STEP 3 below.

.................
.................
STEP 2 of creating a new ADK set of files
.................
.................
cd 4.<new_number>/creation_scripts  to access the following run_.. creation scripts

run_libcomp

This creates a local libcomp.atpglib file from the ../verilog/adk.v  file, 
   as well as important output files to examine.

cat sim.log and make sure "No error between simulated and expected patterns" near the end (rather than mismatches).

For fault coverage, make sure only the file "fault_coverage_100_percent_models" exists, and the file
"fault_coverage_60_to_70_percent_models".  The 4 clock_shaper models are currently in 60-70% file and all other
models are currently in 100% file.  If any other fault_coverage_.. file exists, the models listed in that 
file should be examined carefully.  Also if any other models in 60-70% than clock shapers.
The Verilog is probably bad, although it may be a difficult to test model (such as the clock_shapers). 
Possibly (although not likely), the libcomp.atpglib models listed in that file needs manual intervention
due to inability to translate the model completely and correctly.

.................
.................
STEP 3 of creating a new ADK set of files.  Verifying the Liberty.
.................
.................
A. Make corresponding changes to the liberty/adk.lib file.  There is no automation to do this.

B. Change the search_path at top in BOTH synopsys/synopsys_dc.setup and synopsys/synopsys_pt.setup
   from prerequisites/techlib_adk.tnt/4.<old_number>/synopsys to prerequisites/techlib_adk.tnt/4.<new_number>/synopsys
   in all the serial paths specified there.
   CAVEAT: Do not forget this because there will be no indication until regressions fail.

C. Verify that LC accepts it using (in the same directory as the new ADK Liberty file):
run_lc_shell

See run_lc_shell for comments on how to check that everything is OK.

CAVEAT: The following reuses fastscan.do.cat and overwrites sim.log from run_libcomp, so make sure
        you are done with run_libcomp results, and have examined sim.log before doing this step.
        run_libcomp is the first step of run_all.

D. Verify Liberty against the Verilog by :
  D.1. run/source verify_liberty_step_1  to create only_liberty.atpglib
  D.2. edit fastscan.do.cat from earlier run_libcomp run and change :
   write netlist design.v -verilog -rep -positional   to :
   write netlist design.v -verilog -rep
  D.3. run/source verify_liberty_step_2  to verify Liberty against Verilog

   NOTE : that it will Error unable to load design if port names in Liberty not same as in Verilog.

  D.4. Check bottom of sim.log to ensure no simulation mismatches.
   Note that any Liberty with statetables (clock gaters and synchronizer_cells) as well as clock shapers will have
     0% coverage, and that verification of the Liberty hardware statetables against the Verilog hardware is meaningless 
     for those, because ATPG produced only X (dont compare) for them.
  D.5. diff verify_liberty_step_1.atpglib_last_release verify_liberty_step_1.atpglib 
     to see what Liberty model differences exist.

E. Verify Cadence has no Errors. Currently it has several IQ2 Warnings
  E.1. tco cadence_rtlc_lib_test_adk_rev.tshell
  E.2. cd !$ 
  E.3. pushd data, then cp techlib_adk.tnt/4.<new_number>/liberty/adk.lib .  // Replace old adk.lib in data/ with new
  E.4. popd, then drun (run the in_techlib_adk and mod_techlib_adk target)
  E.5. Check the transcript diffs (for some reason, you will get LM_LICENSE diffs at the top of both transcripts
       although they are the same -- ignore those).

.................
.................
STEP 4 of creating a new ADK set of files
.................
.................
Before making this run, add any tessent attributes (if needed) for new cells to cell.map file in this directory.
Also, add your preferred cell to be used for test insertion to dft_cell_selection file in this directory.
Send mail to don_ross@mentor.com (or doneross@gmail.com if I'm dead) if you are in doubt.

run_fs_tessent
diff fs_tessent_last_release.log  fs_tessent.log

.................
.................
STEP 5 of creating a new ADK set of files.  To help person doing next release.
.................
.................
run clean in this directory to cleanup the intermediate files created.
mv fs_tessent.log fs_tessent_last_release.log  // So next person has something to compare to.
mv verify_liberty_step_1.atpglib verify_liberty_step_1.atpglib_last_release

.................
.................
STEP 6 of creating a new ADK set of files.
.................
.................
tco dts0101261650_check_adk_db_is_complete.tshell and drun with --prerequisite=<this_new_techlib_adk.tnt_directory>
   to ensure all Verilog modules are also Liberty cells and to ensure synopsys/..setup files point to 4.<new_number>


.................
.................
STEP 7 How to run regressions, and update if clean :
.................
.................

pushd <regression_dir>
mkdir regressoin_subdir_for_TOT_ADK
mkdir regression_subdir_for_new_ADK
pushd !$
// Only do following in subdir for new ADK
mkdir my_local_prerequisites 
cd !$
cp -r <dir_where_created_new_techlib_adk>/techlib_adk.tnt .  // or ./techlib_adk.tnt (same thing).
cd techlib_adk.tnt
ls -ld current  // To ensure it points to <new_dir> for this new ADK release.

popd    // Back to where see both regression areas just created (for TOT ADK and new ADK).

// pushd to an all_prods all_libs build and make sure it is up to date
//    Will use that same TOT build in 2 regression areas -- one using TOT ADK, and other using -prerequisite to use new ADK
//    This is the only reliable way I know of to ensure you do not miss fails due to new ADK.
// popd to get back to where regression areas are for the 2 gsubs

// Run at least the following suites :
// pushd to the regression area for the new ADK :
gsub tshell_bscan tshell lbist lbista ijtag fscan edt dfta yielda ALL:tshell ALL:@tshell  -prerequisite ./my_local_prerequisites
// popd then pushd to the regression area for TOT ADK :
gsub <same_suites_as_above> // But with NO "-prerequisite"

If everything looks good (may have to fix some testcases) :
tci techlib_adk.tnt // The one in regression_subdir_for_new_ADK/my_local_prerequisites
tci any testcases that had to be fixed, and any with diffs that need updating.

Else (things are wrong). If you want to tci to save work, BE SURE TO :
ln -sfn 4.<old_number> current
before you tci techlib_adk.tnt
Also change 4.<new_number> to 4.<new_number>_work_in_progress
so it is obvious that it is not released yet.


